1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,417
Lecture Replay Assistant helps students revisit a specific idea in a recorded lesson.

2
00:00:06,417 --> 00:00:12,833
Instead of scanning a whole recording, search the prepared transcript and select a timestamp.

3
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:16,740
This sample is a sixty second synthetic lesson about vectors.

4
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:20,646
It has no audio.

5
00:00:20,646 --> 00:00:24,552
Its twelve bilingual captions were written manually and aligned to the teaching slides.

6
00:00:24,552 --> 00:00:28,458
This is not an automatic transcription result.

7
00:00:28,458 --> 00:00:33,125
Here, searching for span filters the transcript.

8
00:00:33,125 --> 00:00:37,792
Selecting the twenty second result moves the player to the matching slide.

9
00:00:37,792 --> 00:00:42,458
The video timeline and the current caption use the same timestamp.

10
00:00:42,458 --> 00:00:46,458
English search ignores letter case.

11
00:00:46,458 --> 00:00:50,458
Uppercase VECTOR finds the same nine captions as lowercase vector.

12
00:00:50,458 --> 00:00:54,667
Chinese keywords also work.

13
00:00:54,667 --> 00:00:58,875
This search finds the nine captions containing the Chinese word for vector.

14
00:00:58,875 --> 00:01:04,083
If a keyword does not match, the interface shows a clear empty state.

15
00:01:04,083 --> 00:01:09,292
Clearing the search restores all twelve transcript entries.

16
00:01:09,292 --> 00:01:15,569
This walkthrough uses captured screens from the working prototype, with English on-screen explanations and no audio.

17
00:01:15,569 --> 00:01:21,847
Browser playback, search and three timestamp jumps were checked.

18
00:01:21,847 --> 00:01:28,125
AI transcription, concept extraction and Intel Arc Pro B70 deployment remain planned and have not been validated.
